# WhatsApp Deep Link

Use the `whatsapp://` URI scheme to open the app directly. `https://wa.me/` redirects through the browser first.

## URL construction

```js
// ✅ Opens WhatsApp app directly (no browser window)
const waUrl = `whatsapp://send?phone=${phone}&text=${encodeURIComponent(text)}`;

// ❌ Opens browser tab first, then may redirect to app
const waUrl = `https://wa.me/${phone}?text=${encodeURIComponent(text)}`;
```

## Navigation — always use window.location.href

```jsx
// ✅ Stays in app, hands off to WhatsApp
<button onClick={() => { window.location.href = waUrl; }}>
  Enviar por WhatsApp
</button>

// ❌ Forces a new browser tab
<a href={waUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">WhatsApp</a>

// ❌ Also opens browser tab
window.open(waUrl, '_blank');
```

## Phone format

- Strip all non-digits, then prepend country code: `52` + last 10 digits.
- `whatsapp://` scheme does **not** accept `+` prefix — use digits only.

```js
const digits = phone.replace(/\D/g, '');
const full = digits.length === 10 ? `52${digits}` : digits;
const waUrl = `whatsapp://send?phone=${full}&text=${encodeURIComponent(text)}`;
```

## Fallback

If WhatsApp is not installed, `whatsapp://` silently fails on desktop. Acceptable for this app (mobile-first). No fallback needed unless desktop support is explicitly required.
